From 58513eb2c3985d5e303936eff985bb4863d6d63c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:08:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fold-pending: a turn paused for an update settles
 its folded notices; resume no longer re-delivers them

PR #2618 review point 1 (review 5898399987), card t_01a1d6d8bf621f17.

Bug: when a turn that folded pending notices (completions, Kanban wakes) parked for a
Hermes update, unfold_for_checkpoint reverted the folded rows to queued. But the paused
turn's user message (head text + folded texts) is already persisted: the checkpoint
requires a complete persisted tool suffix after the claim, and resume_session_checkpoint
continues that persisted history. The continuation then folded the same rows again, so
the model read each notice twice (once more per further pause). PR #2618's own paused
test encoded this: texts[2] == pause_note(k) + c1 + c2 with history content=event.text.

Fix: the folded rows settle in the checkpoint's own write
(checkpoint_session_input(folded=...), _settle_folded): 'steered' (delivered, acked once)
when a user row of the conversation's chain was written after the claim's
transcript_mark, i.e. the text is durable in the history the continuation resumes; back to
their own FIFO places only when no user row of the turn was persisted. Same transaction,
so _binding's 'steering transfer exists' refusal no longer applies, and a refused
checkpoint rolls the settle back: the claim then settles interrupted and settle_outcome
requeues every folded row as before (the fold entry is released only after commit).
After commit release_checkpointed drops the fold/transfer fences and publishes 'steered'
to each row's observers once (_settle_cancelled, as publish_transfers does).

Proof:
- New invariant test test_a_notice_folded_into_a_paused_turn_reaches_the_model_once
  [user_row|tool_suffix_only]: each folded notice appears exactly once across persisted
  history + every later turn's text, the row settles 'steered', and is published once.
  RED on main for [user_row] (assert (1 + 1) == 1) and for
  test_two_completions_and_a_kanban_row_fold_and_settle_once[paused] (rows 'queued');
  GREEN with the fix (10/10 in the file).
- Mutants (7/7 killed): drop the not-durable requeue branch; drop role='user'; skip
  the settle; drop the steered publish; keep steer_transfers fence; keep the fold entry;
  skip release_checkpointed.
- Consumers: all 20 test files importing the update-pause / fold modules, 164 passed.
